## Summary

The CLI exposes three image modes (default extract / `--keep-original-links` / `--embed-images`) but the **default** is inconsistent across capture methods, and the help text doesn't match observed behaviour. Proposed contract:

> **Default `--format markdown`** for any URL emits markdown that references images by their **direct remote URL** (no `images/` folder, no inline base64). Switching modes requires an explicit flag (`--extract-images`, `--embed-images`).
>
> **Default `--format archive`** emits a zip containing `document.md`, `document.html` (source, for reference), and an `images/` folder with the bytes; the markdown inside the zip references the local files.

Today's behaviour, on Google Docs (4 paths × 3 modes):

| Path           | default          | `--keep-original-links` | `--embed-images` |
|----------------|------------------|--------------------------|-------------------|
| JS-API md      | extracts to disk | **deletes images entirely (alt is empty)** | inline base64 |
| Rust-API md    | **silently inlines base64 (5.9 MB output)** | deletes images entirely | inline base64 |
| JS-browser md  | remote URLs      | flag has **no effect**   | flag has **no effect** |
| Rust-browser md| remote URLs      | flag has **no effect**   | flag has **no effect** |

Only the **browser** paths' default matches the proposed spec ("direct links"). API paths default to extract; browser paths ignore mode flags entirely.

## Why this matters

- A user reading the README expects the same flags to do the same thing on every URL. Today, `--embed-images` is silently a no-op on browser captures.
- Google Docs API capture defaults to a 5.9 MB markdown with embedded base64, even though the user asked for plain `--format markdown`. That's surprising.
- `--keep-original-links` on the API path strips images entirely (alt is `""` for every Google Docs image), so the mode that should be the **safest** on a slow network silently produces image-less output.

## Proposed default contract

| `--format` | Default image handling                  | Files written |
|------------|-----------------------------------------|---------------|
| `markdown` | Direct remote URLs                      | `<output>.md` |
| `archive`  | Local files in `images/` + source HTML  | zip with `document.md`, `document.html`, `images/*` |
| Any       | `--extract-images <dir>`: explicit local extraction | `<dir>/images/*` and rewritten markdown |
| Any       | `--embed-images`: explicit base64        | single self-contained file |
| Any       | `--keep-original-links`: alias for default markdown behaviour (kept for back-compat) | unchanged |

For Google Docs, "direct remote URL" requires **NOT using** `/export?format=html` (which embeds base64). Instead:

- Browser path: already does the right thing — uses `docs-images-rt/<token>` URLs from the editor model.
- API path: switch to the Docs REST API (`https://docs.googleapis.com/v1/documents/<id>`) which returns `inlineObjects[].embeddedObject.imageProperties.contentUri`, OR use the editor model and skip `/export?format=html` for the default markdown route.

